<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Thursday 110,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Thursday 110,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thursday's estimate of interior Iowa/southern Minnesota hog marketings was 110,000 head, compared with 106,000 a week ago and 113,000 a year ago.</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 60 percent Carcass Base Hogs.</p>
<p>Barrows and gilts $0.50 per cwt higher than midsession Wednesday. Trade slow to moderate with good demand and moderate offerings.</p>
<p>				  Country			  Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs		   51.50 -52.50	   52.50 -53.50</p>
<p>liberal volume		52.00 -52.50	   53.00 -53.50</p>
<p>few			     53.00		    54.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs		   49.50 -52.50	   50.00 -53.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs		   46.00 -51.00	   46.50 -52.00</p>
<p>Sows:   generally steady.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs.	 43.50 -46.00	   44.00 -46.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.		  47.00 -48.00	   48.00 -49.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up		   50.00 -54.50	   52.00 -56.00</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 pct carcass yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 pct lean. Special considerations and grade premiums not reflected in base prices.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-983-7347--</p>
